2026-11-01T16:25:05+00:00 session on m34 (the phone's matrix, session 4 (#27, #46, #47): the important cells left, about 2 h 10 min with the fixed 3-minute start waits. B1 in FP32 at 960 against B3 in per-channel INT8 at 1280, back to back (the phone's equal-latency candidate past 1120: session 3 measured B1 FP32 at 960 at 1397.6 ms, and B3 INT8 at 1280 scales to about 1290 ms); then B1 and B2 in per-channel INT8 at 800 (their INT8 speed-up against session 3's FP32 cells at 800). ONNX Runtime only, all 1,610 test-dev images. Seed 5 runs the pair first, so a cut takes the INT8 cells at 800. The rest of the Pi 5's cells moved to session 5): 4 cells; every run uses 4 threads and 20 warm-up images, untimed
